          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Equivariant homotopy theory is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            for the case that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} acts
            on all the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            or other objects involved, hence the homotopy theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-spaces"} topological G-spaces
          %p
            The canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            of topological
            = succeed "-spaces" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopies"} homotopies
            between these are
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+theorem"} Whitehead theorem
            says that on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-CW+complexes"} G-CW complexes
            these
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalences"} homotopy equivalences
            are equivalently those maps that induce
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            on all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            spaces for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroups"} subgroups
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (compact subgroups, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is allowed to be a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elmendorf%27s+theorem"} Elmendorf's theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-presheaves
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#HomotopyTheory"} In topological spaces – Homotopy theory
          %p
            (Beware that
            = succeed "-homotopy" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-actions"} ∞-actions
            of the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
            of
