          %p
            The union of
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is allowed to vary is
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
          %p
            The direct
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilization"} stabilization
            of equivariant homotopy theory is the theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra+with+G-action"} spectra with G-action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spectra"} G-spectra
            and they are the subject of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %p
            The concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of equivariant homotopy theory is
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
