            local
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} model structure on simplicial sheaves
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            be the unit interval, the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            = succeed "-action," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Top
            and hence in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSh(G Top)
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mi Top
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi loc
                    %mi I
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ←
                  %mi sSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mi Top
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi loc
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  sSh(G Top)_{loc}^I  \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to}
                  sSh(G Top)_{loc}
          %p
            for the left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
            at thecollection of morphisms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi Id
                        %mo ×
                        %mn 0
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X \stackrel{Id \times 0}{\to} X \times I\}
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mi Top
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi loc
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSh(G Top)_{loc}^I
            is the equivariant homotopy category described above
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ho
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi sSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mi Top
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi loc
                    %mi I
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi loc
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ho(sSh(G Top)_{loc}^{I}) \simeq G Top_{loc}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#MorelVoevodsky03"}> Morel-Voevodsky 03, example 3, p. 50
            ).
          %h3#global_equivariant_homotopy_theory Global equivariant homotopy theory
          %p
            The above constructions may be unified to apply “for all groups at once”, this is the content of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+equivariant+homotopy+theory"} global equivariant homotopy theory
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion+of+global-+over+G-equivariant+homotopy+theory"} cohesion of global- over G-equivariant homotopy theory
          %h2#in_more_general_model_categories In more general model categories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            as above. We describe the generalizaton of the above story as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            is replaced by a more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (
            %a{:href => "#Guillou06"}> Guillou 2006
            ).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_and_proposition Definition and proposition
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  Let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  be a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
                  with generating cofibrations
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  and generating acyclic cofibrations
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                %p There is a cofibrantly generated model category
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msubsup
                          %mi O
                          %mi G
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi loc
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [O_G^{op}, C]_{loc}
                %p
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
                  from the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+category"} orbit category
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  by taking the generating cofibrations to be
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi O
                              %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi H
                        %mo ×
                        %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                            %mo ,
                            %mi H
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        I_{O_G} := \{G/H \times i\}_{i \in I, H \subset G}
                %p and the generating acyclic cofibrations to be
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi O
                              %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi H
                        %mo ×
                        %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi J
                            %mo ,
                            %mi H
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi G
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        J_{O_G} := \{G/H \times j\}_{j \in J, H \subset G}
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  Let
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                  be the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  and let
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %msup
                          %mi G
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi loc
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [\mathbf{B}G^{op}, C]_{loc}
                %p
                  be the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
                  from
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
                  to
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  – the category of objects in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  equipped with a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                  equipped with a set of generating (acyclic) cofibrations
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mrow
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi H
                        %mo ×
                        %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                            %mo ,
                            %mi H
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        I_{\mathbf{B}G} := \{G/H \times i\}_{i \in I, H \subset G}
                %p and the generating acyclic cofibrations to be
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi J
                          %mrow
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi H
                        %mo ×
                        %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi J
                            %mo ,
                            %mi H
                            %mo ⊂
                            %mi G
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        J_{\mathbf{B}G} := \{G/H \times j\}_{j \in J, H \subset G}
                        \\,.
                %p
                  This defines a cofibrantly generated model category if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %msup
                          %mi G
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbf{B}G^{op}, C]
                  has a
                  %em cellular fixed point functor
                  (see…).
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_and_proposition_2 Definition and proposition
            %p
              %strong (generalized Elmendorf’s theorem)
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi e
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi loc
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G/e \times (-) : C \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} [\mathbf{B}G^{op},C]_{loc} : (-)^e
            %p
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Θ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi O
                      %mi G
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi loc
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ←
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi loc
                    %mo :
                    %mi Φ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Theta : [O_G^{op}, C]_{loc} \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} [\mathbf{B}G^{op},C]_{loc}
                    \: \Phi
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Guillou06"} Guillou 2006, Prop. 3.1.5
          %h3#in_stack_toposes
            In
            = succeed "-stack" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-toposes" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The assumption on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            entering the generalized Elmendorf theorem above is satisfied in particular by every left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi A
                  %mi SPSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C := L_A SPSh(D)
          %p
            of the global projective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
            onany
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            at any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of morphisms, i.e. for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Guillou06"} Guillou 2006, Ex. 4.4
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = \{C(\{U_i\}) \to X\}
            the collection of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cover"} Cech cover
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sieve"} covering families
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models+for+%E2%88%9E-stack+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} models for ∞-stack (∞,1)-toposes
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p
            This way the above theorem provides a model for
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For instance, in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+homotopy+theory"} motivic homotopy theory
                one considers cohomology in a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+localization"} homotopy localization
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
                on the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nisnevich+site"} Nisnevich site
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi Cech
                      %mi SPSh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Nis
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C := L_{Cech} SPSh(Nis)
                \. Its
                = succeed "-equivariant" do
